  "id": "COMPOUND:42560 - PROTEIN:3546",
  "verbalization": "Plastoquinone 1 is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Lactosylceramide alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Plastoquinone 1 acts as a target of Phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate 4-kinase type-2 beta, which in turn is targeted by Ekeberin D4. This chain of targets culminates in the enzyme Lactosylceramide alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, indicating a potential regulatory or enzymatic role for Plastoquinone 1 in the metabolic process of sialylation. The shared pathway and the sequential targeting imply a possible functional link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular network involved, underscoring the need for further investigation into the specific mechanisms by which Plastoquinone 1 influences the activity of this sialyltransferase.",
